# RutaSec Design System

RutaSec is a **Cyber Learning OS**: structured, technical, calm, and progress-driven. The visual direction is **Cybertech Learning Workspace** (Linear + Huly + Pirsch + Slite, with Raycast/Resend polish).

This rule covers **visual design and tokens**. Page structure for catalog/library listings lives in `catalog-information-architecture.mdc`. shadcn primitive usage lives in `ui-shadcn.mdc`.

## Brand personality

**Feel:** technical, calm, focused, practical, structured, premium, developer-first, security-oriented, progress-driven.

**Avoid:** childish UI, over-gamification, generic academy templates, cyberpunk clichés, fake hacker aesthetics, neon green as brand color, matrix effects, skulls, excessive glow on every element, decorative gradient fills on cards and panels.

Cybertech comes from **structure + data + precision + route systems + security language**, not decoration.

## Color tokens

All colors live in `src/styles.css` `:root`. Use CSS variables, never hardcode hex in components.

### Base surfaces

| Token | Usage |
| ----- | ----- |
| `--bg-base`, `--background-soft`, `--background-muted` | Page backgrounds |
| `--surface`, `--surface-raised`, `--surface-hover`, `--surface-active` | Cards, panels |
| `--border-subtle`, `--border-default`, `--border-strong` | Borders |
| `--text-primary`, `--text-secondary`, `--text-muted`, `--text-disabled` | Text hierarchy |

### Brand

| Token | Usage |
| ----- | ----- |
| `--primary-color`, `--primary-hover`, `--primary-active` | Primary actions, active nav, focus |
| `--primary-soft`, `--primary-border`, `--primary-glow` | Soft fills, chip borders, glow |
| `--cyber`, `--cyber-hover`, `--cyber-soft`, `--cyber-border` | Lighter indigo accents, kickers, hero glow |

Indigo is the main identity color. Lighter indigo (`--cyber` / `--primary-hover`) is for secondary accents only.

### State

| Token | Usage |
| ----- | ----- |
| `--success`, `--success-soft`, `--success-border` | Completed checkpoints, success |
| `--warning`, `--warning-soft`, `--warning-border` | In-progress, pending, review |
| `--danger`, `--danger-soft`, `--danger-border` | Errors, blocked, critical |
| `--info`, `--info-soft`, `--info-border` | Informational alerts |

shadcn tokens (`--primary`, `--ring`, `--border`, etc.) map to indigo. Components should prefer design tokens (`--text-primary`, `--border-default`) in Tailwind arbitrary values: `text-[var(--text-primary)]`.

## Typography

| Role | Font | Class |
| ---- | ---- | ----- |
| Display headings | Sora | `.display-title` |
| Body | IBM Plex Sans | default / `font-sans` |
| Technical metadata | IBM Plex Mono | `.type-mono`, `font-mono` |

Use monospace for: route IDs, resource types, skill tags, checkpoint codes, status labels, keyboard shortcuts, kickers (`.island-kicker`).

Do not use monospace for long prose or page titles.

## Spacing and radius

8px spacing system: `--space-1` (4px) through `--space-20` (80px).

| Element | Radius token |
| ------- | ------------ |
| Buttons | `--radius-md` (10px) |
| Cards | `--radius-lg` (14px) |
| Large panels / modals | `--radius-xl` (18px) |
| Badges / pills | `--radius-full` |

Content widths: `--content-narrow` (760px), `--content-default` (1120px), `--content-wide` (1440px).

## Surfaces, glow, and gradients

**Default cards and panels** (`.island-shell`, `.feature-card`, shadcn `Card`) use **solid surface tokens** (`--surface`, `--surface-raised`) with **thin borders** and restrained shadows. Do not add gradient fills to cards, shells, or grid items.

**Gradients are reserved** for scoped, intentional accents only — see `src/styles.css`:

| Location | Purpose |
| -------- | ------- |
| `body`, `body::before` | Page backdrop atmosphere (one subtle layer per page) |
| `.cyber-glow` | Hero / empty-state atmosphere |
| `.brand-mark`, `.nav-link::after` | Small accent details (logo tile, nav underline) |

Do not introduce new gradient backgrounds on components unless you add a named utility class with a clear, single purpose. Never stack multiple gradients on one surface.

**Glow** is reserved for **active or important** elements only:

- `.route-active` — current route highlight
- `.route-completed` — completed route
- `.route-warning` — blocked / warning state
- `.feature-card:hover` — indigo border + `--primary-glow` shadow
- Primary buttons — `--primary-glow` shadow

Default cards use **border**, not heavy shadow. Floating menus and modals may use `--shadow-md` / `--shadow-lg`.

Never apply glow to every card in a grid.

## Component patterns

### Cards

Use shadcn `Card` with `.island-shell` for elevated panels and `.feature-card` for interactive resource entries.

```tsx
<Card className="island-shell rounded-2xl border-[var(--border-default)] shadow-none">
```

Hover: `translateY(-1px)` via `.feature-card:hover` with indigo border and `--primary-glow` shadow. Surfaces stay solid — no gradient fill.

### Buttons

Use shadcn `Button`. Primary actions get indigo fill + `--primary-glow` shadow. Secondary uses border + `--surface`. Ghost for low emphasis.

### Badges

Use shadcn `Badge`. Technical metadata (level, type, status, route ID) uses `variant="outline"` or `font-mono`. Free/success badges use `--success` text on `--primary-soft` background.

### Page headers

```txt
[island-kicker label]
[display-title h1]
[one sentence of practical copy]
```

Copy must answer what the user should do next. Avoid motivational fluff.

### Empty states

Be useful, not decorative:

```txt
No resources saved yet.
Start with the Web Pentesting route and save resources you want to review later.
```

### Progress panels

Compact, data-focused. Simple bars and numbers. Muted grid lines. No chart clutter unless data warrants it.

