| `.nav-link` | Header nav with indigo underline |

## Motion

Default transition: 160ms ease on background, border, color, transform.

Allowed: card hover lift, route node activation, progress completion, drawer transitions.

Avoid: bouncy animation, parallax, glitch effects, gaming-style level-up effects.

## Accessibility

- Maintain strong contrast on `--text-primary` against dark surfaces.
- Do not rely on color alone for status. Pair with text or icon.
- Keep `:focus-visible` outline (2px indigo, 2px offset). Do not remove focus rings.
- Interactive targets must meet minimum touch size.
- Font sizes must remain readable. Avoid tiny low-contrast metadata.

## Content tone

**Use:** "Continue your route.", "Complete the next checkpoint.", "Save this resource.", "Review weak areas."

**Avoid:** "Become an elite hacker.", "Hack the planet.", "Master cybersecurity overnight."

Button labels: Continue route, Start checkpoint, Save resource, Add note, Mark completed.

Status labels: Not started, In progress, Completed, Blocked, Recommended, Saved, Reviewed.

## Do / Do not

**Do**

- Use dark surfaces with thin borders
- Use indigo for primary actions and active states
- Use lighter indigo sparingly for kickers and glow accents
- Use technical badges and monospace metadata
- Use practical, direct copy
- Prefer borders over heavy shadows
- Use solid `--surface` tokens on cards and panels

**Do not**

- Hardcode colors in components (use CSS variables)
- Use teal, neon green, or ocean-themed token names
- Add gradient fills to cards, panels, or list items
- Stack layered gradients on surfaces
- Apply glow to every card
- Use skulls, matrix backgrounds, or fake terminal screens
- Copy Linear/Huly/Pirsch layouts verbatim
- Add decorative sections that do not help learning progress

